Nemesis Firewall — Source-Available License

Copyright (c) 2026 nemesis-sw

1. DEFINITIONS

"The Software" means the Nemesis Firewall source code, object code,
documentation, and associated files contained in this repository.

"Personal Use" means use of the Software by an individual, or within a
single household, for that individual's or household's own network
security — not on behalf of, for the benefit of, or in connection with any
business, organization, or commercial activity, and not for any paid
service offered to others.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is not Personal Use,
including without limitation: use by or on behalf of a business, nonprofit,
government body, or other organization; use to provide a paid or unpaid
service to third parties; use in a commercial product or offering; and use
to protect infrastructure operated for commercial purposes.

"Commercial License" means a separate written license agreement obtained
from the copyright holder authorizing Commercial Use, on terms agreed
between the parties.

2. GRANT — PERSONAL USE

Subject to the terms of this License, the copyright holder grants any
individual a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable
license to:

  (a) view, download, and run the Software for Personal Use;
  (b) modify the Software for that individual's own Personal Use; and
  (c) redistribute unmodified copies of the Software, for Personal Use by
      the recipient, provided this License is included unmodified.

This grant does not include the right to sell the Software, to relicense
it, to remove or alter this License, or to use it for Commercial Use.

3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A SEPARATE LICENSE

Commercial Use of the Software requires a Commercial License from the
copyright holder. This includes any deployment mode of the Software that
is marketed, documented, or offered as intended for commercial or
business use, REGARDLESS of whether the Software technically enforces
that restriction in a given mode or configuration. Where the Software
does not technically prevent a particular Commercial Use, this License is
the only thing that makes that use unauthorized — the absence of a
technical block is not permission.

To inquire about a Commercial License, contact: license@nemesis-sw.com.

4. SOURCE AVAILABILITY IS NOT AN OPEN-SOURCE GRANT

The Software's source is made available in this repository for
transparency, security review, and community trust — so that anyone can
verify what a security product installed on their own network actually
does. This availability is NOT an open-source license under any OSI
definition, and does not by itself grant rights beyond Sections 2 and 3
above. In particular, availability of the source does not grant the right
to build a competing product or service from it, whether free or paid,
outside the scope of Section 2.

5. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL
THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY
ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE.

This Software is a network security tool, not a guarantee of security.
See the product documentation for its stated scope and limitations.

6. TERMINATION

This License terminates automatically if you breach any of its terms.
Sections 4 and 5 survive termination.

